{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>For they are small</b> — an adjective with the noun missing, like: \"and he spoke to them harshly.\"" "<b>And the word 'despise'</b> — from עלומי העי\"ן (with hidden [quiescent] ayin), like: \"they do not despise the thief.\" And here it is: \"For who has despised the day of small things,\" or [it means] small deliverances, and this is the missing noun, like: \"and he spoke to them harsh words.\" When they see the plummet stone, which is the tin stone in Zerubbabel's hand for building the House — behold, seven eyes shall guard it, so that no one approaches to cast it down. And it is possible: seven eyes — many guards. And another interpreted: just as the angel interpreted, \"these seven are the eyes of HaShem,\" and the angel explained that the seven are the eyes of HaShem, which roam throughout all the earth." "<b>And the meaning of 'seven'</b> — in the manner of \"and he called it Shib'ah,\" and \"Shevu'ah\" is derived from \"seven,\" as he said: \"for there both of them swore\" — in the manner that the author of Sefer Yetzirah mentioned, and the Sanctuary Hall is aligned in the middle. And this requires a long explanation, for there it is written that the six directions are above and below, front and back, right and left, and the Sanctuary Hall is aligned in the middle, and this is part of the explanation: for everything has the six directions that he mentioned, and the Sanctuary Hall is the Debir, which has these directions and is aligned in the middle. And they called it the Sanctuary Hall — it is the honored middle one, and it is the master of the directions, for from it are the directions and to it they belong. And this matter encompasses all created beings, and concerning that which is more honored, he mentioned 'Hall of the Holy of Holies.'"], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {1 "Reading הבדיל ('tin') per the standard text; the phrase עלומי העי\"ן is translated hyper-literally as Ibn Ezra's technical description of the ayin in בז being quiescent/hidden."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:05.252222458Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}